# Files exposed read-only at /AOK/native/libs/helix, embedded into the kernel
# by tools/gen-aokfs.py at build time (see meson.build / fs/aok.c).
#
# /AOK/native/libs is the support-file area for NATIVE PROGRAMS: things a
# program compiled into the app has to read at runtime and cannot fetch,
# because there is no package manager on this side of the boundary and nowhere
# writable that survives an app update.
#
# Unlike the /AOK/tests, /tools and /docs manifests, names here nest as deeply
# as they like. The directories are DERIVED from these paths rather than
# declared in fs/aok.c, which is what makes a tree this shape possible: helix
# alone is a directory per language.
#
# Each line: <path> [mode]   read from deps/helix/runtime/<path>, served at
#                            /AOK/native/libs/helix/<path>.
#
# helix is the first tenant. Its tree-sitter queries are what turn a linked-in
# grammar into actual colour -- the grammar parses, the queries say what to
# paint -- and the themes are what `:theme` has to offer. Only the queries for
# the languages deps/rust-native links a grammar for are here; a query file
# with no grammar behind it would be dead weight.

